==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Crazed Princess Punt CC''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Manic Princess Punt''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Crazed Princess Punt is unique in how she rushes forwards like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Express Cat]] would, yet she attacks from a very long distance as well. She is better used in strategies that involve a drawn out fight, as that is the only real way for her presence to be noticeable, with her very low DPS and long attack rate. Having one of her around while a stack of metal enemies slowly push can usually make a big difference, but that is pretty much all she can do.

If using her, make sure to protect her, as she has low health and a somewhat long recharge time.

==='''True Form'''===
The extra range and quicker attack rate help her a lot, allowing her to generally last longer and build up the damage she ends up doing before dying to something somewhat worthwhile.

The best thing, however, is the combination of that with her increased chance to knock metals back, as that results in a unit who is able to keep the odd metal enemy at bay while the cat army takes care of the others first.

==='''Talents'''===
Target Zombie and Zombie Killer cost a lot and give little return, as zombies can easily take her out, while she can barely damage them, making these talents not recommended. As a result of her unimpressive health and damage, their respective buffs will usually just be a waste of NP.

Lastly, the only talent worth considering is the chance to crit. It may not be much, but for a unit who can stall out metal enemies well, a full wipe every once in a while of the weaker ones definitely has value.

